{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505739180,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTg0Njg1MDc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842","origin":"github"},"title":"Make ConfigManager deal with empty strings in config items","message":"First and foremost this is about using env variables to set datalad config items.\nAs seen in PR #1841, there is a need to a general solution on how to approach this.\nAt the very least an env variable set like `SOME_THING=` is to be treated as if it wasn't set at all, I think, which means the value we get from `ConfigManager` likely shouldn't be an empty string.\nHowever, it also might not be a good solution to always return `None` in that case.\nATM I think this should be dealt with in the constraints, that are used to define the domain of the config item in `common_cfg` and then consequently use `ConfigManager.obtain()` instead of its `get()`, so that the conversion by those constraints actually takes place. That way, an item expected to be an integer can be considered to be `None` in case of an empty string, while for an item expected to be string, it might still be okay to simply stick with the empty string.","files":null}]}